# The Tower's long texts, one a line (src/game/tower/tower.c's TXT_ keys, in order): every BoonId, the six affixes, the seven Offerings, then the Codex's pages (segments split by '|': '#' a heading, '%' grey, '!' red, '+' after a gap, '~' a new page, '@' the page's table). No line breaks inside a text.
Your damage +15% a level at Lv 1-3, then +10% a level at Lv 4-5 (+65% at Lv 5).
Damage taken -15% a level at Lv 1-2, and -10% more at Lv 3 (about -35% in all).
+3 to the run's most potions a level, and 3 potions now (15 at most).
Potions heal 25% more a level (a potion heals 45% of max health before boons).
Rolls cost 40% less stamina.
Stamina refills 40% faster a level, and an empty bar waits less before it refills.
Skill cooldowns -20% a level (x0.8 each level: x0.51 at Lv 3). Offered once a skill is known.
Each sword hit heals 12% a level of its base damage (a sword hit of 4 heals 0.5 a level). Skills and lightning don't heal.
+25 max health a level, and 25 health at once.
Below 30% health your damage is +40% a level.
Once a floor, a killing blow leaves you at 1 health instead.
Perfect dodges are easier: the first 0.28 s of a roll count (0.20 without it). Each perfect dodge heals 2% of max health.
A perfect dodge gives +50% damage for 2.5 s.
A staggered boss stays down 50% longer.
A staggered boss takes +60% damage. The stagger bonuses add up, +100% at most.
Every 4th sword hit calls a bolt of lightning on the boss (6 damage).
Your damage +35%, and potions heal 25% less.
Health a blow takes can be won back by hitting the boss: each hit wins back a quarter of its base damage (Lv 2: half). It waits 1 s (Lv 2: 1.5 s), then drains away over 4 s.
The combo's 3rd hit makes the boss bleed 4 a level over 3 s (a tick every 0.5 s); another finisher adds to it. It heals nothing.
Drinking a potion gives +25% damage for 6 s.
+10% damage a level for every full 25% of your health missing.
With Storm Blade: its bolts +1.5 a level. Without it: every 8th sword hit calls a bolt of its own (6, +1.5 a level above Lv 1).
The combo's 3rd hit calls a bolt of lightning (6).
Lightning fills the boss's stagger meter as a sword hit does. Offered once something calls lightning.
When the boss is staggered, your next 5 sword hits each call lightning.
Each sword hit takes 0.3 s a level off every skill cooldown. Offered once a skill is known.
A skill's hit on a staggered boss deals +50% (the stagger bonuses add up, +100% at most).
Each skill cast gives the sword +15% damage for 4 s.
The combo's 3rd hit fills the stagger meter 20% more a level.
A blow that would take over 20% of your max health deals 25% less.
Any roll gives +8% damage a level for 2 s.
A perfect dodge gives the roll's stamina back.
After 3 perfect dodges on a floor, the next blow that lands deals nothing (once a floor).
+20% gold a level, from every source: fights, Skip, the purse and the Events.
Below half health: a blow that doesn't knock you down can't flinch you or break a skill's wind-up; each sword hit in a row +8% damage, up to +40% (a blow taken or 2 s without a hit ends the streak); and no potions.
Leap and send 5 crosses round you (0.8 each, about 4 a cast; they fill the stagger meter like one sword hit). Cooldown 15 s.
Charge 2 s, then a wide slash in front (28). A blow during the charge breaks it. Cooldown 45 s.
5 blades fly out in a fan, each hitting up to 4 times (about 13 a cast). Cooldown 18 s.
10 crosses of 2 each (about 20 a cast); the first five keep Lv 1's stagger.
7 crosses of 1.75, each filling the stagger meter like two thirds of a sword hit: the heart of a stagger build.
A second slash 0.35 s after the first, the same arc at 40% of its damage and stagger.
The slash all the way round you, x1.15 damage, 60% stagger; blows don't break its charge or slash (their damage still lands).
3 more blades follow the middle three 0.3 s behind, at 70% damage (8 blades a cast).
Blades fly 1.6x as far and hit 6 times, in a narrower fan, to hit from range.
The combo's 3rd hit deals +25%.
The first blow each floor deals half.
Storm Blade's lightning comes every 3rd hit (was every 4th).
A staggered boss takes +90% (was +60%).
When a staggered boss rises, its stagger meter doesn't drain for 3 s.
Riposte's +50% lasts 4 s (was 2.5 s).
When Unbroken saves you, you also heal 20% of max health.
Bloodthirst heals 16% a level of a hit's base (was 12%).
Rally wins back three quarters of each hit's base (a sword hit 3).
The perfect dodge's window is 0.31 s (was 0.28 s).
Storm Blade's and Static's bolts deal +50%.
Thunderclap's bolt deals +50% (9).
Moon Mastery cuts 25% a level (was 20%: x0.42 at Lv 3).
With Bloodthirst, each bolt of lightning heals at half its rate (of the bolt's damage); without it, bolts deal +25%.
A perfect dodge calls two bolts on the boss, 0.3 s apart (Storm Blade's, with Static's bonus).
Each skill cast costs 3% of max health (never the last of it), and skills' hits deal +40%.
When the boss is staggered, every skill cooldown is ready again.
A perfect dodge opens Riposte's window (2.5 s); hits in it win back 60% of their base of the health blows took (on top of Rally's share).
Lightning on a staggered boss deals double.
A perfect dodge takes 2 s off every skill cooldown.
Each potion drunk: +10 max health for the floor (up to +30) and -40% damage taken for 4 s.
A skill's first hit each cast calls Storm Blade's pillar on the boss (6).
footwork, breathers and cooldowns 20% faster; strikes keep their timing.
+30% health, a stagger bar 30% longer.
below half health, blows +25%, shorter breathers.
its stagger drains 2x, it rises in 2.5 s, shorter breathers.
heals 25% of the health its blows take.
slams and dives leave fire for 2-3 s.
Start the next climb with one more potion, and its most potions one higher: a Shop sells one further.
+10 max health for the whole climb. A potion heals a share of max health, so each one heals a little more too.
Start the next climb with 60 gold: a Mend, a potion or a Common boon at its first Shop.
+25% damage until the first circle is cleared, when its Guardian Unbound falls.
The climb's first draft holds two skill cards: choose which skill to learn, or a level of the one you know. Nothing with Skills off.
The climb's first Rest heals 40% of max health on top of whatever you take there.
Start the next climb holding a random Common boon at Lv 1, in a slot (never Deep Flask). Release it at a Rest if it doesn't suit you.
Each floor is one fight. Fall, and the climb ends: its gold and boons are lost, its Embers kept.|A circle is one map, from the Guardian to Guardian Unbound. Each circle the bosses grow stronger, and so do you, through the fifth.|#Your belt|A fallen boss gives a potion, even past your most, up to 15. Health isn't given back between floors.
Seven rows, three lanes, from the bottom up. The Guardian opens a circle and Guardian Unbound ends it, after a Rest on every lane. Your path holds 4 to 6 fights.|#Moving|Left and Right pick a node. A shows its page, A again enters, B goes back. B on the map: the pause menu.|#Nodes|Fight: a Bonus boss.|!Elite: a stronger one, for a richer draft.|Event: a choice. Shop: spend gold. Rest: heal, Temper or potions.
A Fight is a Bonus boss, met once a circle while any are left; only they come as Elites.|!Elites: x1.25 health and an affix, two from the fourth circle.|They pay a Rare-or-better draft and x1.5 gold and Embers; with two affixes, a duo if one is ready.
#Rest|Heal 40%, Temper a level, or +2 potions. Then Release a boon if you wish, free.|#Shop|Each item once a visit:|@|#Events|A choice on the way; you can always walk on. None comes twice in a climb while others wait, and more wait deeper in.
Five slots. A new boon takes one at Lv 1; the same card again is its next level.|Full, drafts offer only what you hold: levels, "+", duos, skills and pacts.|Release frees one: free at a Rest, 20 gold at a Shop.|%Skills and pacts take none.
Every boon is of a family, named in its colour on the card. Hold two of a family and its boons come twice as often.|@
Take one, and its rival is locked out for the climb, even if you release it. A skill's two forms are rivals too.|@
#"+"|A boon at its most can rise once more: its "+". No slot.|#Duos|With a maxed boon of each of two families, their duo can come. It merges both into one slot (both keep working) and opens the other.|%It goes only as a whole, and needs both families' packs.|@
Learned only in the climb. The Learn card is Lv 1, the same card again the next level, up to Lv 4. Then a draft offers its two forms: take one, lose the other.|Until one is known, every draft leads with a Learn card; then one in three holds a skill card.|%Each skill's second form is bought at the Shrine.
