Named on the map and over the health bar; the boss's body, timing and sound tell the rest.|@
For this climb only, lost when it ends.|@
Banked as each boss falls, and kept for good.|@|#The Shrine|Upgrades for every climb. Relics: one worn a climb. Unlocks: new boons and the skills' second forms.|%Offerings and Milestones: their own pages.
Gifts for the next climb only, from the Tower's menu: two at most, the second 50 Embers more. Prices never rise.|Used as the climb starts. Quit before its first Guardian falls and they wait for the next climb; fall, and they're spent.|@
Your best floor earns these, for good.|@
A blessing bound to a curse, for the climb. No slot: they stack without end. Every Shop holds one, free: the curse is the price.|@
From the second circle, each circle has a night: a burden, and more Embers.|@
The Demon King raised the Tower from his throne's own stone.|Every knight who fell in it still keeps its halls: hollow armour, made whole each time someone climbs.|The bosses are never slain. The Tower lets them sleep, and wakes them stronger.|%You have climbed further than any knight before you.
